  "level": "L2",
  "title": "Scheduler queue fallback and chunk budgets retain distinct selection behavior",
  "mechanism": "The configured LPM or HRRN policy can return an active FCFS policy when the waiting queue exceeds its configured threshold. However, calc_priority checks the configured self.policy for the explicit FCFS sorting branch; the active-policy fallback reaches a pass branch and preserves existing queue order. Thus the threshold fallback is not evidence of a newly sorted FCFS queue. Prefill budget evaluation distinguishes NO_TOKEN for memory or Mamba exhaustion from OTHER for input, diffusion-model or chunk limits. Replay can reduce the effective chunk limit, and later alignment rounds a permitted chunk down to the required boundary; a successful budget check need not admit the full remaining request.",
  "corrections": [
    "Do not equate the active fallback label with execution of the configured-FCFS sort.",
    "Keep memory/token exhaustion separate from other scheduling-budget limits.",
    "The accepted subset establishes source decisions only, without throughput or starvation measurements."
  ],
  "source_scope": "Manually read the listed exact Git ranges for the final corrected mechanism. All other model claims remain research notes; no runtime experiment.",
